Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 19:55:20 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 410/443] [ae-patch] Voice mode on iPhone and iPad transcribes
 on the box instead of Apple's recognizer

Apple's recognizer goes deaf after any spoken reply on iOS 18. A Voice mode start on iPhone or iPad now uses the server dictation stream (default on, per-device switch Transcribe on the box). Manual mic taps keep the browser path. The dictation session skips the sample-rate hint on iOS, resumes its audio context, reuses one context unlocked inside the Voice tap, logs timings and levels, and restarts once (then reports deaf) when a take hears only silence. The level meter no longer opens a second capture on such a take. The Voice sheet's keyboard button now lines up with End.
